From e9a908b2a02b6a22dc383f223b7aa792913b875f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:39:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] Round 3: Serialize typed full-record metrics directly

The domain now returns typed catchment and reservoir metrics structs
instead of nested serde_json::Value maps built with string keys for
every record. Fields are declared in sorted key order, so full-record
JSON text is unchanged and the CLI's Value view is identical; a unit
test checks both. The unused Failure metrics hook is removed. The
benchmark accepts CRAFT_WORKERS to override a workload's worker count
for scaling studies; workload definitions are unchanged when unset.

Workload: serial (96 full records, one worker), 11 samples against
round 2.
Before median: 0.595 ms. After median: 0.359 ms. Speedup: 1.66x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
